// A direct call to a nested `fn` BEFORE its declaration in the same fn body. The checker hoists the
// nested declaration (collect.rs pass 1), so this type-checks; the runtime must agree by binding the
// block's `fn` declarations before the block's other statements run. Previously this aborted with a
// runtime E0005 ("cannot find `g`") — a checker/runtime hoisting mismatch, now fixed in the shared IR
// lowering (the same fn-hoist the module top level already applies), so both backends agree.
// expect: stdout "7"
// expect: exit 0
fn outer(): int {
    x = g();
    fn g(): int { return 7; }
    return x;
}
echo outer();
